    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n89" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăbĭtĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		abeo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				going away</i>, <i>departure.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen. (ante-class. for
			abitus), <i><span class="en">Plaut. Rud. 2, 6, 19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ter. Heaut.
				1, 2, 16</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In partic., = mors, <i>death</i>, acc. to
			Gloss. ap. Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p. 380, 9</span></i>
		Müll.</div>
